BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (      The First Villager approached the bridge carrying grain. Fear whispered, "What if they kee) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (        p it all?" But courage won. She carried seventy portions across-a great share of her har) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (        vest.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (      When she arrived, the grain had become two-hundred-ten portions. The Second Villager faced) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (         his own test. "I could keep everything," Greed murmured. But Wisdom spoke louder: "She ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (        trusted you with her sustenance.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (      The Second Villager returned half the bounty. The First Villager went home richer than bef) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (        ore, and the Second Villager kept abundance for his people.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (      The bridge taught them: trust must be met with fairness. Those who send much deserve retur) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (        n. Those who receive must honor the gift.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
