BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (        ayal-it is simply silence.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (      She chose patience over judgment. She maintained the bridge, kept the path clear, and wait) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (        ed. For one cannot return what was never received, but one can preserve what was once sh) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (        ared.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (      The next season, grain appeared again on the bridge-perhaps the mists had cleared, perhaps) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (         the storms had passed. The magic worked as before, tripling the trust. The daughter ret) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (        urned generously, showing that one season's silence had not broken the bond.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (      The elders learned: "The covenant is not measured in single crossings, but in the willingn) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (        ess to maintain the bridge through all seasons. Empty crossings test our patience; abund) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (        ant crossings test our generosity. Both reveal our character.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
