BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (    The keeper watched the dark water in the eighth season, uncertain if her single candle from ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (      the seventh had been swallowed by the void like so many offerings before.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (    Then-a flicker. Small, wavering, but real. A flame crossing back to her shore.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (    It was not the bonfire of abundance from seasons past. It was not even the steady torch she ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (      had sent. But it was light. It was answer. It was the other village saying: "We are still ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (      here. We still remember the bridge.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (    The keeper gathered her council. "They sent what they could through the terrible mists. Perh) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (      aps they too are depleted from seasons of uncertainty. Perhaps the fog distorted what reac) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (      hed them, just as it distorted what reached us.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (    She divided the returned light carefully-half to honor their effort, half to restore her own) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (       stores. Not the generous overflow of early seasons, but fair recognition that both villag) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      es were struggling through the same obscuring fog.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (    "What now?" her people asked.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (    "Now we watch," she said. "They lit a torch when they could barely see. I answered it fairly) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (      . If this proportional exchange continues-small lights carefully tended, fairly shared-per) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (      haps we can rebuild what the mists have obscured. Not all at once, but flame by flame, unt) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (      il the bridge glows bright again.") Tj ET
BT /F2 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (  Agent_2 \(Briar\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (    Myth: The Torch Sent, The Response Awaited) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (    The daughter kept her word. In the seventh season, she sent her torch into the mist-not a bo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (      nfire that would exhaust her village, but a clear, measured flame that said "I am here.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (    She waited by the shore for an answer. When dawn came, the waters brought nothing. The keepe) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (      r across the bridge had spoken of sending "a single candle," yet no light had arrived. Per) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (      haps the mists had swallowed it. Perhaps the candle was never lit. Perhaps their story spo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (      ke of intentions while the current spoke of choices.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (    The daughter felt the weight of it-the distance between the myths we tell and the offerings ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (      we send. But she did not let bitterness take root.) Tj ET
